<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
  <!ENTITY name      "tollroll">
  <!ENTITY slug      "tollroll">
  <!ENTITY author    "Junker der Provinz">
  <!ENTITY version   "1.2.2">
  <!ENTITY launch    "Settings/tollroll">
  <!ENTITY gitURL    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/junkerderprovinz/tollroll/main/plugin">
  <!ENTITY pluginURL "&gitURL;/&slug;.plg">
  <!ENTITY pkgURL    "https://github.com/junkerderprovinz/tollroll/releases/download/v&version;">
  <!ENTITY emhttp    "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&slug;">
  <!ENTITY plgPath   "/boot/config/plugins/&slug;">
  <!ENTITY txz       "&slug;-&version;-x86_64-1.txz">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;"
        author="&author;"
        version="&version;"
        launch="&launch;"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        min="6.12.0"
        support="https://github.com/junkerderprovinz/tollroll/issues">

<!-- The name is the lowercase slug so Unraid finds the logo
     (plugins/<slug>/images/<slug>.png) and the Plugins tab description
     (plugins/<slug>/README.md); the display name comes from README.md. -->
<ICON>
/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&slug;/images/&slug;.png
</ICON>

<CHANGES>
One dashboard tile for the apps of your fortress: a row per app with how it is
doing, and one log with the lines of all of them, filtered by a click. It joins
the fortress with its phrase and reads the status report every member serves.

### 1.2.2
Info shows where TollRoll's updates stand, What's new opens in a window, and every notification channel gets Edit and an on/off switch.

✨ **Added**
- **Version in Info.** It shows TollRoll's number and where its updates stand, as the Plugins tab sees them. Check for updates runs the same check the Plugins tab runs, and once a new version is out, Update in the Plugins tab takes you there. Until Unraid has checked once, the card says Not checked yet.
- **What's new opens in a window.** It holds the notes of the version you run, or of the new one while it waits in the Plugins tab. The notes come from the plugin on your server, so your browser asks GitHub for nothing.
- **Components in Info.** The GlimStone version TollRoll is built on has a card of its own.
- **Edit and switch off a channel.** Edit opens a channel's fields in the same window you added it in, with a switch to turn it off, and an Off channel says so on its row.

🎨 **Design**
- **Channels as connection rows.** Each channel shows its service's mark, its name and what it sends, then Test, Edit and Remove.
- **Version numbers are plain text.** A number opens its project's newest release, and on a phone a long one moves under the name.
- **GlimStone 4.9.0.**

⚡ **Improved**
- **kit 1.1.0.** Your fortress membership, channels and settings carry over as they are.

🌐 **Translations**
- **Every new text in all 26 languages Unraid offers.**

### 1.2.1
Names in the channel window and on the buttons in Info keep their descenders.

🐛 **Fixed**
- **Tile names keep their descenders.** The bottom of a g, p or y in a tile's name in the channel window is no longer cut off.
- **GlimStone 4.7.0.** The buttons under Help and About in Info keep their descenders too.

🌐 **Translations**
- **Dutch says inloggen and login for signing in,** as the other apps do.

### 1.2.0
The watch learns from you: mark a finding as known, or keep it as a real incident with a note. It also looks at more of your server, and the logs of your containers, plugins and user scripts get rows of their own on the tile. Thanks to @Revan335, whose questions in [#3](https://github.com/junkerderprovinz/tollroll/issues/3) started it.

✨ **Added**
- **Is known or Real incident.** Every finding of the watch has two buttons in the Open view and in the status window. Is known takes it as normal, and TollRoll does not report the same again. Real incident keeps it with your note, and for 30 days TollRoll tells you right away when the same thing comes from the same source, even during the quiet hours.
- **Containers with special rights.** A container that runs privileged, on the server's own network or with Docker's socket gets a line in the log, once for each right.
- **Unusual disk traffic.** When a disk reads or writes far more in an hour than it usually does, the log says so. TollRoll learns what is usual from the kernel's counters, so it wakes no disk, and it leaves parity checks and the mover out.
- **Snapshots that vanish.** ZFS or btrfs snapshots that are gone, with no app of your fortress having logged their removal, get a line of their own. TollRoll lists snapshots only on pools that are awake.
- **New jobs in the at queue.** A job TollRoll has not seen before gets a line, once.
- **Logs of containers, plugins and user scripts.** They get rows of their own, Containers, Plugins and User Scripts, and their lines are sorted into errors, warnings and info like the syslog's, with the info lines folded away. TollRoll reads only the end of each log, and a container's log only while the disk Docker lives on is awake.
- **Mute until.** Pick a time, and until then only alerts go out. When it ends, one message sums up what waited.
- **All quiet.** Switch it on, and on a day when nothing happened a short message says so at the time of the daily summary.

🎨 **Design**
- **Open points stand apart.** Points in the Open view and the status window, and the suggestions in the settings, each sit on a surface of their own with a gap between them, and the buttons of a finding are filled.
- **Channels from GlimStone's catalog.** In the window that adds a channel, mail shows SMTP as its second line, a search for Element finds Matrix, and the webhook comes last. Back from a channel's form marks the tile you picked before.
- **GlimStone 4.6.0.** With TowerTorch, quiet buttons in the channel window hover in its accent colour, and open lists keep TowerTorch's plain rows.

⚡ **Improved**
- **The tile opens on the log.** The Everything view is gone, since the Apps view shows the rows and the list at the top of the log picks the apps. A tile that was set to Everything opens on the log.
- **A busy app leaves room for the others.** Every app keeps its newest lines in the log, however much another one writes.

🐛 **Fixed**
- **Icons take the colour of the text around them,** so none turns black on a dark tile.

🌐 **Translations**
- **Every new text in all 26 languages Unraid offers,** and the French texts say tu throughout.

### 1.1.0
Your server and your router write into the tile's log in plain words, and a notification hub sends the messages of every app in your fortress through one set of channels, with quiet hours and a daily summary. Thanks to @Revan335 for the idea in [#3](https://github.com/junkerderprovinz/tollroll/issues/3).

✨ **Added**
- **Your server in the log.** Unraid's syslog joins the tile's log, sorted into errors, warnings and info. Lines that matter, such as disk errors, parity checks, the mover, sign-ins or running out of memory, come with one sentence that says what they mean, and a parity check says why it started. Hover a line to see the original, and routine noise folds into one line.
- **Disks that wake up.** When an array or pool disk spins up, the log says which one and what likely woke it: a container, a VM, a network share, the mover, a parity check or a scheduled task. Pick Disks above the log and press Open to see how often each disk woke today and in the last 7 days. TollRoll only reads, so it never wakes a disk itself.
- **The unusual stands out.** A sign-in from a new address, a burst of failed sign-ins, a new plugin, changed settings on the flash drive, a new scheduled task, a share newly open to guests or many files deleted at once get a line of their own. When /var/log is 80% full, the log names the biggest file and who writes it.
- **Your router's log too.** Send it to Unraid's syslog server, and TollRoll watches it for new sign-ins, changed port forwards and firewall rules, intrusion warnings, new devices on your network and a log that goes quiet. It only reads those lines and never connects to the router.
- **A notification hub.** Send messages to Unraid, Apprise, Discord, Gotify, Matrix, ntfy, Slack, email or a webhook. Apps of your fortress that know TollRoll hand their notifications to it, so quiet hours, a daily summary and a level per app apply to all of them. The same message goes out once, and a flood of them waits for the next free slot.
- **The all-clear reaches every channel.** When an app says a problem is over, channels that only take problems hear it too.
- **Messages lead to the right page.** A message can link to a page on your server, and every channel opens it under your server's address.
- **Suggestions.** TollRoll looks at your server and suggests an app of the fortress where one would help, for backups, container updates or the server's health.
- **Everything open in one view.** Open in the tile header lists what each app still needs from you.
- **Plugins that only check now and then** still get their row on the tile.
- **The Help card** offers the TollRoll Discord server beside GitHub.

🎨 **Design**
- **Channels picked from tiles.** Add a channel in a window with a search and the services' logos, then fill in its fields and send a test right there. Every change is saved at once.
- **A real time picker** for the quiet hours and the daily summary: pick the hour and the minute from two lists.
- **Cleaner settings.** Fields have no frames, every button shows its icon, controls stand at the end of their row, open lists show plain rows with a check mark, and the (i) and its bubble look like they do in your other apps.
- **GlimStone 4.5.7.** With TowerTorch, rows, chips, views, options and tabs light in its hover colour, and the chosen view and filter above the log take your accent colour.
- **Without a fortress** the tile header holds only the title and its buttons.

⚡ **Improved**
- **A steadier fortress.** TollRoll keeps listening on a server with a single network interface, a member that already took a new phrase no longer shows as gone, and a member that is just closing no longer locks out a newcomer.

🐛 **Fixed**
- **The gear in the tile header** is as easy to see as the other header buttons with TowerTorch.

🌐 **Translations**
- **Every new text in all 26 languages Unraid offers,** and French readers are addressed with tu.

### 1.0.0
Your whole fortress on one dashboard tile, with one log for every app. Joining takes twelve words, and you never type an address.

✨ **Added**
- A dashboard tile with a row per app of your fortress: its state, what needs you, what it is working on and its version. An app that runs on several devices still gets one row.
- One log with the lines of every app, newest at the bottom. Click an app, or its button above the log, and the log shows only its lines.
- Open in the tile header shows the chosen app's status window, with what needs you, what it is working on, what comes next and its latest log lines. For the app's own pages, open it in BombVault, KnightLoader or ArrowLoop, wherever you are.
- Your other apps can open TollRoll's status window too. It shows TollRoll's version, its next check and a log of what it told you.
- Join your fortress with its phrase under Settings → Utilities → TollRoll. Every app in the same fortress then shows up by itself, whether it runs on this server or on another device.
- Your other apps show TollRoll with its own logo.
- When your fortress moves to a new phrase, TollRoll follows on its own and stays the same member, so no duplicate shows up. If it can't, the settings page asks for the new words.
- If another app takes TollRoll out of the fortress, the settings page says so, after a restart too, and once the phrase has changed, lets it back in with the new one.
- Take any other member out of the fortress right from the settings page. TollRoll asks first, then points you to an app where you change the phrase, because until you do, your fortress takes no new app. Until then, a quiet line names who you took out, and an app that tries to join is told why.
- Four views in the tile header: everything, the apps alone, the log alone and a map of every device with its apps. The tile keeps your view and your pick of apps on the server, so every browser finds it the way you left it.
- Notifications through Unraid, Apprise or Matrix when an app stops answering, answers again or newly needs you. Each one goes out once, so a long outage does not fill your inbox.
- Every setting is saved the moment you change it. Only the twelve words wait for the Join button.
- TollRoll keeps only the keys made from your phrase, never the phrase itself. The browser talks to the Unraid WebGUI alone. At home the other apps reach the service behind it directly, relay or not, on a port that lets in fortress members and nobody else.

🎨 **Design**
- Each row wears the app's own logo and colour from its status report, or its first letter when the report has none. A logo is checked and only ever drawn as an image, so nothing in it can run.
- The log keeps its dark terminal look on every Unraid theme.
- The settings page has the same tabs as our other Unraid plugins: General, Notifications, Fortress and Info, with the version, help and a way to say thanks.
- The fortress card is the same in every one of our Unraid plugins and has its own tab, right above Info. It shows each app with its logo, how it runs and its version, and Open tells you how a plugin is doing.

🌐 **Translations**
- Every text in all 26 languages Unraid offers. Texts from your apps arrive in your language too, as far as each app has them.
</CHANGES>

<!-- Pre-install: stop the service, then prune packages of older versions only
     and keep the current one cached. On a reboot Unraid reinstalls each .plg
     before the network is up, so the cached &txz; on the flash is what lets the
     reinstall work offline. mkdir -p first, because on a fresh install the
     directory does not exist yet and find would end the install. -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
&emhttp;/scripts/rc.tollroll stop 2>/dev/null
mkdir -p &plgPath;
find &plgPath; -maxdepth 1 -name '*.txz' ! -name '&txz;' -delete 2>/dev/null || true
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!-- The package (service binary and webgui files) is built by
     plugin/pkg_build.sh and attached to the GitHub release "v&version;". CI
     writes the SHA256 at release. upgradepkg removes files a newer package
     dropped. -->
<FILE Name="&plgPath;/&txz;" Run="/sbin/upgradepkg --install-new --reinstall">
  <URL>&pkgURL;/&txz;</URL>
  <SHA256>7550ea36311d767f248a51151648e74e5105e0e1b14bc901a2c2a4dd1584ca73</SHA256>
</FILE>

<!-- Post-install: start the service. It runs on every boot as well, since
     Unraid reinstalls every plugin then. -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
chmod -R u+rwX,go+rX &emhttp; 2>/dev/null
chmod +x &emhttp;/bin/&slug; &emhttp;/scripts/rc.tollroll 2>/dev/null
&emhttp;/scripts/rc.tollroll start
echo ""
cat &emhttp;/banner.txt 2>/dev/null
echo ""
echo "TollRoll is ready!"
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!-- Remove. The plugin manager runs only FILE elements and ignores a bare
     REMOVE, and the block has to end with exit 0, or Unraid keeps the .plg and
     reinstalls it on boot. The settings on the flash stay, so a reinstall
     keeps the fortress membership and the notification channels. -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
cat &emhttp;/banner.txt 2>/dev/null
echo ""
echo "Bye!"
echo ""
&emhttp;/scripts/rc.tollroll stop 2>/dev/null
pkg=$(ls /var/log/packages/ 2>/dev/null | grep -E "^&slug;(-[^-]+-[^-]+-[^-]+)?$" | head -n1)
if [ -n "$pkg" ]; then removepkg "$pkg" 2>/dev/null; fi
rm -rf &emhttp;
rm -f &plgPath;/*.txz /var/run/&slug;.pid /var/run/&slug;.sock
echo "TollRoll removed. Your fortress membership and notification channels in"
echo "&plgPath; were kept. Delete that folder if you do not plan to reinstall."
exit 0
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
